<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk oil port closed - source.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk oil port closed - source.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea was shut for most of the weekend due to high winds and swell and remained closed on Monday morning, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The terminal, which shut at 1800 (local) on Friday, reopened early Sunday morning allowing two tankers to berth but then closed again at midday (local).</p>
<p>Five tankers were at anchor outside the port on Monday.</p>
<p>The port of Tuapse was also shut because of bad weather but Odessa and the Baltic port of Ventspils were operating normally, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
